---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getSupabaseClient } from '../lib/supabase';

const supabase = getSupabaseClient();
const { data: settings } = await supabase.from('site_settings').select('contact_email').single();
const contactEmail = settings?.contact_email ?? null;

const LAST_UPDATED = '17 September 2026';
---

<Layout title="Terms — JTP Skulptur" description="The terms and conditions for using the JTP Skulptur website and purchasing sculpture or prints.">
  <header class="mx-auto max-w-(--measure-full) px-4 pt-14 sm:px-8 sm:pt-20">
    <p class="caption">Legal</p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-3 text-3xl sm:text-5xl">Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-(--measure-content) px-4 py-10 sm:px-8 sm:py-14">
    <p class="caption">Last updated {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

    <div class="mt-6 border-l-2 border-(--color-clay) pl-6 text-sm leading-relaxed text-(--color-ink-soft)">
      <p>
        These terms cover use of this website and purchases made through it. They have been drafted from the site's
        current functionality and are <strong>not</strong> a legally reviewed document. Sections marked
        {' '}<strong class="text-(--color-clay)">[Confirm]</strong> describe policies (shipping windows, returns,
        governing law, and similar) that have not yet been finalised, and must be reviewed by the site owner — ideally
        with legal advice — before this page is relied upon or launched publicly.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">About these terms</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      By browsing this website or placing an order, you agree to these terms. If you don't agree with them, please
      don't use the site or place an order.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Using this website</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      This website and its content — images, text, and design — belong to JTP Skulptur or the respective artist,
      unless otherwise noted. You may browse and share pages of this site, but you may not copy, reproduce, or
      reuse images or content without permission.
      <strong class="text-(--color-clay)"> [Confirm]</strong> exact intellectual-property ownership and any
      agreements with featured studio partners.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Artworks &amp; products</h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-3 leading-relaxed">
      <li>
        Many works offered here are original, one-of-a-kind sculptures. Once a piece is sold, it's marked as no
        longer available and cannot be purchased again.
      </li>
      <li>
        Availability shown on the site reflects our records at the time, but isn't guaranteed until your payment is
        confirmed — in rare cases (for example two near-simultaneous orders for the same unique piece), an order may
        need to be cancelled and refunded if the piece is no longer available.
      </li>
      <li>
        Prices are shown in the currency displayed at checkout.
        <strong class="text-(--color-clay)"> [Confirm]</strong> whether prices include or exclude VAT/sales tax, and
        who is responsible for import duties on international orders.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Ordering &amp; payment</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Checkout and payment are handled entirely by Stripe on Stripe's own secure payment page. An order is only
      confirmed once payment has been successfully processed, at which point you'll receive an order confirmation by
      email.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Shipping &amp; delivery</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-(--color-clay)">[Confirm]</strong> Shipping carriers, estimated delivery windows per
      region, packaging/insurance for fragile or high-value pieces, and who bears responsibility for customs or
      import charges on international orders. Shipping regions and rates currently offered at checkout are shown in
      your cart before you pay.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Returns, refunds &amp; damaged items</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-(--color-clay)">[Confirm]</strong> This section is not yet defined and needs the site
      owner's input before launch — particularly given that many works are unique, one-of-a-kind sculptures. At a
      minimum this should cover: whether returns are accepted and within what period, the process for a piece
      damaged in transit, and how refunds are issued.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Studio partners</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Some items on this site are supplied by independent makers or studios ("vendors") featured alongside JTP
      Skulptur's own work.
      <strong class="text-(--color-clay)"> [Confirm]</strong> who is the seller of record for these items — JTP
      Skulptur or the individual maker — as this affects which consumer-rights obligations apply.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Liability</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-(--color-clay)">[Confirm]</strong> A jurisdiction-appropriate limitation-of-liability
      clause has not yet been drafted here.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Governing law</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      <strong class="text-(--color-clay)">[Confirm]</strong> Which country's law governs these terms, and where
      disputes would be handled.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display mt-12 text-xl sm:text-2xl">Contact</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      {contactEmail ? (
        <>Questions about these terms can be sent to <a href={`mailto:${contactEmail}`} class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">{contactEmail}</a>.</>
      ) : (
        <>Questions about these terms can be sent via our <a href="/contact" class="text-(--color-clay) hover:underline">contact page</a>.</>
      )}
    </p>
  </div>
</Layout>
